@host = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### List every order
GET {{host}}/orders

### Filter by status (ASSIGNED | REASSIGNMENT_PENDING | REASSIGNED | DELIVERED)
GET {{host}}/orders?status=ASSIGNED

### Unknown status -> 400 with a field violation
GET {{host}}/orders?status=BOGUS

### Create an order (201; increments the agent's activeOrderCount)
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ORD-009", "description": "Flowers — Frazer Town to Cooke Town", "assignedAgentId": "AGT-002" }

### Duplicate id -> 409
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ORD-001", "description": "Duplicate", "assignedAgentId": "AGT-002" }

### Unknown agent -> 404
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ORD-010", "description": "Orphan parcel", "assignedAgentId": "AGT-999" }

### Ask the active routing strategy where ORD-001 should go (201)
### Creates a PENDING suggestion and moves the order to REASSIGNMENT_PENDING.
POST {{host}}/orders/ORD-001/suggest

### Repeat the same suggest -> 409, the state machine refuses a second pending suggestion
POST {{host}}/orders/ORD-001/suggest

### Which routing strategy is active, and what is registered?
GET {{host}}/routing/strategy

### Switch the active strategy at runtime — takes effect on the next call, no restart
PATCH {{host}}/routing/strategy
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "rule-based" }

### Switch to the AI strategy (T-3) -> 200, active becomes "ai" on the next routing call
### With no GEMINI_API_KEY set this still succeeds: "ai" activates, and each routing call then
### degrades to rule-based, so the suggestion above comes back with strategyUsed "rule-based".
### The WARN line naming the fallback reason is in the application log.
PATCH {{host}}/routing/strategy
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "ai" }

### Unregistered strategy -> 409, the previous strategy stays active
### "ai" is registered since T-3, so this probe needs a key nothing answers to.
PATCH {{host}}/routing/strategy
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "zone-affinity" }

### Update agent availability (AVAILABLE | BUSY | OFFLINE)
### T-1 only records the status; reassigning that agent's orders is T-4.
PATCH {{host}}/agents/AGT-001/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "OFFLINE" }

### Accept a reassignment suggestion
### Requires the order to be REASSIGNMENT_PENDING — run the suggest request above first.
PATCH {{host}}/suggestions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "ACCEPTED" }

### Reject a suggestion (order stays REASSIGNMENT_PENDING)
PATCH {{host}}/suggestions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "REJECTED" }
